{number: 128}
{title: Are You Washed in the Blood?}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] Have you been to Jesus for the cleansing pow'r?
Are you washed in the [Db] blood of the [Ab] Lamb?
Are you fully trusting in His grace this hour?
Are you washed in the [Eb7] blood of the [Ab] Lamb?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Are you [Ab] washed in the blood,
In the [Db] soul-cleansing blood of the [Ab] Lamb?
Are your garments spotless? Are they white as snow?
Are you washed in the [Eb7] blood of the [Ab] Lamb?
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Are you [Ab] walking daily by the Savior's side?
Are you washed in the [Db] blood of the [Ab] Lamb?
Do you rest each moment in the Crucified?
Are you washed in the [Eb7] blood of the [Ab] Lamb?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
When the [Ab] Bridegroom cometh will your robes be white?
Are you washed in the [Db] blood of the [Ab] Lamb?
Will your soul be ready for the mansions bright,
And be washed in the [Eb7] blood of the [Ab] Lamb?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Lay a-[Ab] side the garments that are stained with sin,
And be washed in the [Db] blood of the [Ab] Lamb;
There's a fountain flowing for the soul unclean,
O be washed in the [Eb7] blood of the [Ab] Lamb!
{end_of_verse}
